+It searches for jobs, then fills forms until the day's number is reached or
+a limit stops it. In prepare mode, the default, it prints what is ready for
+your approval, what needs you, and what could not be prepared; with
+`"mode": "send"` it prints what it sent, what waits for you, and what it
 could not send. The same summary is kept in `data/runs/daily-<date>.json`.
 
+`--send` sends what is ready for this one run, whatever the mode says;
+`--prepare` prepares, whatever the mode says.
+
 `--target 5`, `--max-attempts 10` and `--max-minutes 30` tighten one run.
 `--no-discover` uses the queue as it is.
 
+## Approving prepared forms
+
+With `"mode": "prepare"`, or no `mode` at all, a run fills and checks each
+form exactly as a sending run does, then **sends nothing**. A form that is
+ready stays open in the tool's Chrome window, is recorded as waiting for your
+approval, and the run prints `npx jev submit <id>` for it. This is the same
+for `daily`, scheduled or typed, `apply --submit` and `resume --submit`.
+`apply --dry` is a rehearsal as before. A scheduled run uses the policy's
+mode, so the schedule needs no change.
+
+`/daily approve`, or `npx jev status`, lists three groups:
+
+- **Ready for your approval.** Read the open form, then say which to send.
+  Only the forms you name are sent, with `npx jev submit <id>`. The form is
+  checked again just before the click, and an application counts only when
+  the page after the click is a confirmation.
+- **Needs you.** A robot check, an emailed code, a sign-in. The form is open
+  for you, as in any run.
+- **Could not be prepared.** Set aside with the reason, and on the by-hand
+  list.
+
+A CAPTCHA that only appears when Submit is clicked cannot be seen while a
+form is prepared. It shows when you approve that form, and the form then
+waits for you to pass it.
+
+Limits that differ from a sending run: at most 10 forms are left open at
+once (`DAILY.maxAwaitingApproval`), counting forms still waiting from
+earlier runs, so a day you skip does not pile up more. A form waiting for
+your approval is kept 30 hours (`RUN.approvalExpiryHours`), then closed and
+put on the by-hand list. The per-employer and per-board limits still apply,
+and there is no pause between forms because nothing is sent.
+
